00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:01,330
Then Denver.

92
00:03:01,330 --> 00:03:03,610
And a thin slice in New York.

93
00:03:03,670 --> 00:03:06,214
More than half of America's gold sits

94
00:03:06,214 --> 00:03:09,357
behind one set of doors in Kentucky.

95
00:03:09,617 --> 00:03:11,675
So the gold is real,

96
00:03:11,675 --> 00:03:14,367
and it is enormous.

97
00:03:14,427 --> 00:03:16,413
The strange part is the price written

98
00:03:16,413 --> 00:03:17,667
next to it.

99
00:03:18,117 --> 00:03:25,033
If you like finding the hidden money behind the headlines, hit subscribe and like. It really helps the channel.

100
00:03:36,284 --> 00:03:37,504
For a long time,

101
00:03:37,504 --> 00:03:40,314
the dollar was defined in gold.

102
00:03:40,314 --> 00:03:41,823
From nineteen hundred,

103
00:03:41,823 --> 00:03:43,791
an ounce was worth twenty dollars and

104
00:03:43,791 --> 00:03:45,484
sixty-seven cents.

105
00:03:45,614 --> 00:03:47,125
In nineteen thirty-four,

106
00:03:47,125 --> 00:03:49,229
the government raised it to thirty-five

107
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:50,584
dollars an ounce.

108
00:03:50,584 --> 00:03:52,316
That one change cut the gold value

109
00:03:52,316 --> 00:03:55,285
of the dollar to about fifty-nine percent

110
00:03:55,285 --> 00:03:57,122
of what it had been.

111
00:03:57,384 --> 00:04:00,764
Then came two laws in quick succession.

112
00:04:00,794 --> 00:04:03,406
In March nineteen seventy-two,

113
00:04:03,406 --> 00:04:05,516
Congress set the price at thirty-eight

114
00:04:05,516 --> 00:04:06,644
dollars.

115
00:04:06,754 --> 00:04:09,953
And in September nineteen seventy-three,

116
00:04:09,953 --> 00:04:11,912
it raised it one last time,

117
00:04:11,912 --> 00:04:14,744
to forty-two and two-ninths dollars.

118
00:04:14,894 --> 00:04:17,290
That is forty-two dollars and twenty-two

119
00:04:17,290 --> 00:04:18,544
cents an ounce.

120
00:04:18,744 --> 00:04:20,873
The same law also started to end

121
00:04:20,873 --> 00:04:23,838
the ban on Americans owning gold.

122
00:04:24,084 --> 00:04:24,942
And then,

123
00:04:24,942 --> 00:04:26,104
nothing.

124
00:04:26,104 --> 00:04:28,022
The market price of gold went its

125
00:04:28,022 --> 00:04:28,717
own way,

126
00:04:28,717 --> 00:04:32,194
but the official price never moved again.

127
00:04:32,214 --> 00:04:34,431
It is still written into federal law

128
00:04:34,431 --> 00:04:35,434
today.

129
00:04:35,434 --> 00:04:37,994
Every ounce in Fort Knox is booked

130
00:04:37,994 --> 00:04:41,409
at forty-two dollars and twenty-two cents.

131
00:04:41,650 --> 00:04:44,090
Let me draw two prices on the

132
00:04:44,090 --> 00:04:45,290
same chart.

133
00:04:45,290 --> 00:04:47,799
The official price climbs in small steps,

134
00:04:47,799 --> 00:04:49,826
then goes flat after nineteen

135
00:04:49,826 --> 00:04:51,440
seventy-three.

136
00:04:51,740 --> 00:04:54,250
The market price leaves it behind.

137
00:04:54,490 --> 00:04:56,386
At the end of September twenty

138
00:04:56,386 --> 00:04:57,207
twenty-five,

139
00:04:57,207 --> 00:04:59,314
the market paid about three thousand eight

140
00:04:59,314 --> 00:05:02,020
hundred and twenty-five dollars an ounce.

141
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:03,493
By our calculation,

142
00:05:03,493 --> 00:05:06,157
that is about ninety times the official

143
00:05:06,157 --> 00:05:06,961
price.

144
00:05:07,217 --> 00:05:09,385
Why would anyone keep such an old

145
00:05:09,385 --> 00:05:10,527
number?

146
00:05:10,757 --> 00:05:12,377
Because that number is not just a

147
00:05:12,377 --> 00:05:13,337
label.

148
00:05:13,357 --> 00:05:15,399
It is tied to real money at

149
00:05:15,399 --> 00:05:17,020
the central bank.

150
00:05:22,684 --> 00:05:24,581
In nineteen thirty-four,

151
00:05:24,581 --> 00:05:26,982
the Gold Reserve Act made the Federal

152
00:05:26,982 --> 00:05:28,904
Reserve hand all its gold to the

153
00:05:28,904 --> 00:05:30,224
Treasury.

154
00:05:30,534 --> 00:05:31,398
In return,

155
00:05:31,398 --> 00:05:34,434
the Fed received gold certificates.

156
00:05:34,584 --> 00:05:36,576
They are written in dollars,

157
00:05:36,576 --> 00:05:38,845
and they cannot be swapped back for

158
00:05:38,845 --> 00:05:39,697
gold.

159
00:05:39,950 --> 00:05:42,463
The Congressional Research Service

160
00:05:42,463 --> 00:05:44,180
explains the trick.

161
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:47,111
The Treasury monetized the gold by issuing

162
00:05:47,111 --> 00:05:49,175
those certificates to the Fed,

163
00:05:49,175 --> 00:05:51,052
and the Fed put the money into

164
00:05:51,052 --> 00:05:53,320
the Treasury's own bank account.

165
00:05:53,730 --> 00:05:55,160
But there is a limit.

166
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:57,625
The certificates can never be worth more

167
00:05:57,625 --> 00:05:59,663
than the gold's official value.

168
00:05:59,917 --> 00:06:01,852
That is why the numbers match so

169
00:06:01,852 --> 00:06:03,177
closely.

170
00:06:03,317 --> 00:06:06,011
The Federal Reserve's weekly balance sheet

171
00:06:06,011 --> 00:06:08,257
shows a gold stock of about eleven

172
00:06:08,257 --> 00:06:09,357
billion dollars,

173
00:06:09,357 --> 00:06:12,276
and a gold certificate account of eleven

174
00:06:12,276 --> 00:06:14,897
point oh three seven billion dollars.

175
00:06:15,087 --> 00:06:17,091
The gold has already been turned into

176
00:06:17,091 --> 00:06:17,619
money,

177
00:06:17,619 --> 00:06:20,041
at the nineteen seventy-three price.

178
00:06:20,284 --> 00:06:22,144
Let me draw the loop.

179
00:06:22,144 --> 00:06:23,852
Here is the Treasury,

180
00:06:23,852 --> 00:06:25,194
with the gold.

181
00:06:25,204 --> 00:06:27,414
Here is the Federal Reserve.

182
00:06:27,694 --> 00:06:29,882
The Treasury sends certificates to the

183
00:06:29,882 --> 00:06:30,664
Fed.

184
00:06:30,784 --> 00:06:32,751
The Fed sends dollars back into the

185
00:06:32,751 --> 00:06:34,444
Treasury's account.

186
00:06:34,714 --> 00:06:37,664
The gold itself never moves.

187
00:06:37,764 --> 00:06:40,648
Only the paper and the money do.

188
00:06:40,884 --> 00:06:41,696
Of course,

189
00:06:41,696 --> 00:06:43,935
all of this only works if the

190
00:06:43,935 --> 00:06:45,934
gold is really there.

191
00:06:45,984 --> 00:06:47,652
So who checks?

192
00:06:53,317 --> 00:06:55,170
In nineteen seventy-four,

193
00:06:55,170 --> 00:06:56,815
after questions in Congress,

194
00:06:56,815 --> 00:06:59,313
the Government Accountability Office

195
00:06:59,313 --> 00:07:01,787
