196
00:07:01,847 --> 00:07:04,075
Auditors checked three of the thirteen

197
00:07:04,075 --> 00:07:05,167
vault compartments,

198
00:07:05,167 --> 00:07:07,327
and found no differences.

199
00:07:07,427 --> 00:07:08,210
The next year,

200
00:07:08,210 --> 00:07:10,818
the Treasury set up a permanent committee

201
00:07:10,818 --> 00:07:12,823
to keep auditing the gold.

202
00:07:13,084 --> 00:07:14,671
By nineteen eighty-six,

203
00:07:14,671 --> 00:07:17,081
about ninety-two percent of the gold had

204
00:07:17,081 --> 00:07:18,484
been audited.

205
00:07:18,494 --> 00:07:20,924
And since nineteen ninety-five,

206
00:07:20,924 --> 00:07:23,625
the Treasury's inspector general has

207
00:07:23,625 --> 00:07:26,571
audited the gold in deep storage every

208
00:07:26,571 --> 00:07:27,528
single year,

209
00:07:27,528 --> 00:07:29,738
checking the seals on all forty-two

210
00:07:29,738 --> 00:07:31,074
compartments.

211
00:07:31,104 --> 00:07:33,552
Its latest report gave the Mint a

212
00:07:33,552 --> 00:07:35,240
clean opinion.

213
00:07:35,484 --> 00:07:38,174
Official visits make the news.

214
00:07:38,394 --> 00:07:40,581
In August twenty seventeen,

215
00:07:40,581 --> 00:07:43,776
Treasury Secretary Steven Mnuchin flew to

216
00:07:43,776 --> 00:07:45,742
Fort Knox with Senate leader Mitch

217
00:07:45,742 --> 00:07:46,834
